22d8f1d1-587c-4b17-9d0f-518c7f1f3d0e	Assignment.pdf	323331	application/pdf	circulars	22d8f1d1-587c-4b17-9d0f-518c7f1f3d0e/Assignment.pdf	Assignment	Vivekananda College of Engineering & Technology Assignment\r\nVCET\r\n[A unit of Vivekananda Vidyavardhaka Sangha, Puttur ®]\r\nAI\r\nAffiliated to Visvesvaraya Technological University, Belagavi\r\n22/04/2026\r\nApproved by AICTE, New Delhi & Govt of Karnataka\r\nAssignment\r\nDept: AI Sem: 6th Sub: Machine Learning S Code: BAI602\r\nDate: 22/04/2026 Max Marks: 10\r\n-\r\nQN Questions Marks RBT CO's\r\n1 Consider the training dataset in table below. Construct decision trees using ID3, 04 L3 CO4\r\nC4.5, and CART.\r\n2 Consider an example of predicting a student's result using Gaussian Naïve 04 L3 CO4\r\nBayes algorithm for continuous attribute. The training dataset T consists of\r\n10 data instances with attributes such as 'Assessment Marks', 'Assignment\r\nMarks' and 'Seminar Done' as shown in Table 8.18. The target variable is\r\nResult which is classified as Pass or Fail for a candidate student.\r\nGiven a test data to be (Assessment Marks = 75, Assignment Marks = 6,\r\nSeminar Done = Poor), predict the result of the student.\r\n3 Explain in brief about the advantages and disadvantages of ANN 02 L2 CO5\r\n[Note: Submit it on or before: 01/05/2025]\r\nFaculty in charge: Ms. Vaishnavi K V\r\nNehru Nagar, Puttur - 574 203, DK, Karnataka State – INDIA.\r\nPhone :+91-8251-235955, 234555 Fax : 236444, Web: www.vcetputtur.ac.in,E mail:principal@vcetputtur.ac.in	{}	AIML	circular	11	\N	1	t	deleted	{"all_dates": [], "manual_due_date": null, "auto_extracted_date": null, "extracted_text_length": 1310}	2026-08-21 13:13:38.975089+05:30	2026-09-22 06:05:22.825611+05:30
